# Control Harness Template

This directory is the **outer control harness** for a project generated by
`fulcra-rapid-prototype`. It governs milestones, independent evaluation,
and user decisions, and provides a local, portable scaffold plus explicit
integration extension points for durable Fulcra Workspace tracking. It is
distinct from the generated project's inner runtime model/tool loop
(`engine/`).

**Scope note:** this scaffold now provisions the documented durable Workspace
baseline from this control harness's own contents: root team files, static
spec/decision/governance/milestone/schema artifacts, Generator/Evaluator
member role/progress/inbox state, milestone progress, and status summary.
`run_milestone.py` persists generator reports, candidates, verdicts, decision
requests, status, milestone progression, and full-history Git bundles when
invoked with `--team`/`HARNESS_TEAM`; optional PR-create/merge commands are
injectable host adapters. It includes bounded role wall-clock/retry behavior
and transient provider-limit classification.
Activity-aware watchdogs and a concrete PR-host adapter remain project
integration work, not hidden assumptions.

## Boundaries

- **Control harness:** this directory — portable policy, roles, schemas,
  milestones, and decision/knowledge artifacts. No deliverable source code
  and no execution history.
- **Workspace:** `team/<team-name>/` in Fulcra File Store — durable inboxes,
  status, verdicts, decisions, escalations, and milestone progress. The
  scaffold provisions the baseline role/progress/inbox/control-artifact
  layout; role execution adds terminal verdict/decision/escalation records.
- **Deliverable:** the scaffolded project itself, in a separate git repo.

## Bootstrap

```bash
./bootstrap.sh <team-name> --deliverable <path>
```

This provisions a minimal, real Fulcra Workspace team (root
`role.md`/`progress.md`/`completed.md`/`log.md`, via
`coordinator/bootstrap.py`) from only this control harness's own contents
-- no old inboxes, no local cache. Run `./doctor.sh` afterward (and any
time you resume on a fresh machine) to confirm the harness is actually in
a runnable state before trusting it with real milestone work.

## Provider adapters

`coordinator/run_milestone.py` deliberately does not hardcode Gemini,
Claude, Hermes, or any other agent runner. Provide two external commands:

```bash
export HARNESS_GENERATOR_CMD='your-agent-runner ...'
export HARNESS_EVALUATOR_CMD='your-independent-evaluator ...'
python coordinator/run_milestone.py --milestone M1 --deliverable ../project
```

### Codex CLI OAuth adapter

The included `adapters/codex_role.py` invokes an already-authenticated Codex
CLI session. It does not read or store an OpenAI API key: ChatGPT/Codex OAuth
is usable by the Codex CLI, not by the public OpenAI API used by this skill's
inner runtime adapter. Install the Codex CLI, authenticate once with
`codex login --device-auth`, then configure separate Generator and Evaluator
processes:

```bash
export HARNESS_GENERATOR_CMD='python3 /path/to/control-harness/adapters/codex_role.py'
export HARNESS_EVALUATOR_CMD='python3 /path/to/control-harness/adapters/codex_role.py'
./doctor.sh
```

The coordinator gives each process its role, milestone, immutable spec,
context, and deliverable through `HARNESS_*` environment variables. The
adapter keeps Generator and Evaluator separate, asks Generator to commit only
its milestone branch, and requires Evaluator to emit the structured verdict
lines required by this harness.

Each command receives `HARNESS_ROLE`, `HARNESS_MILESTONE`,
`HARNESS_SPEC`, `HARNESS_CONTEXT`, and `HARNESS_DELIVERABLE` environment
variables. Generator may make coherent incremental commits on only its
milestone branch, then identifies its clean final candidate with the required
`Harness-Candidate: <candidate-id>` commit trailer. The Coordinator evaluates
its exact SHA. On PASS, the Coordinator creates a non-fast-forward merge
commit named `harness/<milestone>: complete milestone`. Evaluator must write a
verdict matching `schemas/verdict.md`.
`run_milestone.py`
enforces `test_runner: PASS` as a merge gate when a test runner is declared,
persists terminal Workspace records with `--team`, and invokes optional
`HARNESS_PR_CREATE_CMD` / `HARNESS_PR_MERGE_CMD` adapters after remote
push/PASS. For an active `create_and_publish` dashboard, also set
`HARNESS_DASHBOARD_REFRESH_CMD`; it receives the team, milestone, outcome, and
decision-file path after each terminal outcome and performs the curated
refresh/manifest gate. A remote merge adapter must create a merge commit (never
fast-forward or rebase) and use `HARNESS_MERGE_MESSAGE`. Provide those adapters for your git host;
the scaffold does not hardcode a specific hosting API.

## Git modes, candidates, and portable history

GitHub is optional. `--git-mode local` (or `HARNESS_GIT_MODE=local`) requires
only local Git branches and integrates a PASS candidate with a mandatory
non-fast-forward merge commit. `--git-mode remote` adds `origin` push plus optional PR
adapters. Set `--integration-branch` / `HARNESS_INTEGRATION_BRANCH` when it
cannot be safely inferred.

Every evaluation candidate has a required, searchable commit trailer such as
`Harness-Candidate: harness/m2-candidate`; the Coordinator records that
identifier/SHA/commit range in the Workspace and evaluates the fixed SHA,
never a mutable branch head.

After every non-dry harness run, the Coordinator uploads full-history bundles
for both the control harness and deliverable to
`team/<team>/artifact/git-bundles/<milestone>/`. The stable `*-latest.bundle`
names intentionally replace older copies because the newest full bundle
already contains its repository history. Retain older bundles only when a
separate audit/archive requirement justifies their storage cost.

The default retention target is **three versions per bundle path**. The
Coordinator never deletes older versions until the user has explicitly
approved pruning for the project and that decision is recorded in
`decisions.md`. Then set `HARNESS_BUNDLE_PRUNING_APPROVED=1` (or pass
`--approve-bundle-pruning`) and provide a trusted `HARNESS_BUNDLE_PRUNE_CMD`.
It receives `HARNESS_BUNDLE_TEAM`, `HARNESS_BUNDLE_MILESTONE`,
`HARNESS_BUNDLE_PATH`, and `HARNESS_BUNDLE_RETENTION=3`, and must remove only
versions older than the retained newest three. The portable `fulcra-api` CLI
currently exposes version inspection/restoration but no delete-one-version
command, so this deliberately remains a platform-specific adapter rather than
guessing at File Store internals.

See `RUNBOOK.md` for the full step-by-step operating flow,
`roles/generator.md` and `roles/evaluator.md` for role responsibilities, and
`roles/manifest.md` for active roles.

## Non-negotiable rules

- Only the user changes `spec.md` and `decisions.md`.
- Generator and Evaluator are genuinely separate sessions/processes.
- Work one milestone at a time; never ask one run to build the whole spec.
- Evaluator runs declared deterministic tests and emits exact
  `test_runner: PASS|FAIL` and `overall: PASS|FAIL` lines.
- A branch merges only after independent PASS.
- A blocking `decision_request: true` pauses work and is surfaced to the
  user; it is never guessed or retried automatically.
